  "title": "Week 40: TLU Japanese Cafe",
  "date": "2025-09-25T21:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Week 40: TLU Japanese Cafe\n\nLast week I finally joined TLU’s Japanese Cafe! 🍵✨\nI had wanted to attend since last year, but back then my schedule clashed with the event. This time, no conflicts — so I went straight in!\n\n🃏 How it Works\n\nWe were divided into small groups. On each table there were cards with questions written in both Japanese and English — great little icebreakers! ⏱️ When the timer rang, we switched groups and topics.\n\nSome sample topics:\n\nWhat part-time job would you take? 💼\n\nWhat car do you wish to have? 🚗\n\nOne Japanese student even shared that she works as a maid in a café — everyone found it super interesting!\n\n🍱 Japanese Evening\n\nAnother highlight was the Japanese Evening. People shared food, stories, and even taught us some dances. 💃🕺 The most surprising part? Some students wore their traditional clothes — really added to the vibe! 👘\n\n🇨🇳 vs 🇯🇵 Events\n\nI’ve also attended Chinese events organized by both the Mainland and Taiwan governments. Honestly, those were a bit too serious 🤓 compared to the Japanese ones. The Japanese side feels much more relaxed, fun, and effective in cultural exchange. Truly, they’re advanced in culture exporting. 🌏✨\n\n🎥 Here’s a short clip from the event:",
